// valid object with <hex> its serialization under the other scheme (under
// the decode scheme it serializes as the input). A class ending in _basic
// re-encodes the first sample of another class in the basic layout. SB gives
// SetBytes under the basic flag with no round trip: I, V (the object B
// yields), or V:<legacy hex>/<basic hex> for an object B does not yield.
//
// pairs: a and b are [class, ops]. The first op builds the object:
// unser:S (Unserialize under S), new:S (default object built while the
// global flag is S) or set:XY (Set the object canonical under X, or the
// invalid one, with scheme Y); get then calls Get. ab and ba give [a == b or
// b == a, a's then b's serialization afterwards], each order on fresh
// objects. Serializations are tags: raw (the input), zero, or XY (the eager
// decode under X serialized under Y). Untagged outputs are hex.
